      <Layer queryable="1">
        <Name>1</Name>
        <Title><![CDATA[BLM Natl Trails Not Assessed for Public]]></Title>
        <Abstract><![CDATA[BLM Natl Trails Not Assessed for Public are a route regarded and or managed as a trail by the BLM for which no BLM travel planning decision has been made as part of a TMP, LUP or other planning decision. No record of decision (ROD) applies to this route. A trail is usually intended for human-powered, stock, or off-road vehicle forms of transportation, or for historical or heritage values. Trails are not generally for use by four-wheel drive or high-clearance vehicles. General Business Rule: A "Not-Assessed-Trail" is correctly classified if; the linear feature looks or functions as a trail but has no associated planning decision; or is actively managed for public access; has a record in the Facility Asset Management System (FAMS), or is published in maps or brochures to promote public use, or any combination of the above. These data are provided by Bureau of Land Management (BLM) "as is" and may contain errors or omissions. The User assumes the entire risk associated with its use of these data and recognizes that this data will never be 100% QCed. Official and accurate data should be obtained directly from the data steward. Please see the metadata of the individual layers for complete details.]]></Abstract>
